    },
    {
      "id": "europe",
      "text": "By the following June, snow was falling in New England and crops were failing across France and Germany. Bread riots followed. Nobody yet understood why.",
      "pause_after": 0.6,
      "text_zh": "第二年六月，新英格兰在下雪，法国和德国的庄稼纷纷绝收。随之而来的是面包暴动。没有人知道为什么。",
      "clips": [
        {
          "image": "assets/03_europe.jpg",
          "motion": "zoom_out"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "legacy",
      "text": "Out of that cold, wet summer came Frankenstein, written by Mary Shelley while trapped indoors by the rain. One eruption, one lost harvest, one monster that never died.",
      "pause_after": 0.6,
      "text_zh": "在那个又冷又湿的夏天，玛丽·雪莱被雨困在屋里，写出了《弗兰肯斯坦》。一次喷发，一季绝收，一个不死的怪物。",
      "clips": [
        {
          "image": "assets/04_legacy.jpg",
          "motion": "pan_left"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "vei",
      "label": "How big was it",
      "text": "On the Volcanic Explosivity Index, Tambora scores a seven. Krakatoa, the eruption everyone remembers, only a six.",
      "text_zh": "在火山爆发指数上，坦博拉是七级。而人人都记得的喀拉喀托，只有六级。",
      "label_zh": "它有多大",
